<h2 style="margin:0 0 12px;font-size:18px;">Respondent traffic is up</h2>

<p style="margin:0 0 16px;font-size:15px;">
  <strong><%= @count %></strong> <%= "response".pluralize(@count) %> in the last
  <strong><%= @window_minutes %> minutes</strong> — about
  <strong><%= @per_minute.round %> a minute</strong>.
</p>

<% if @rows.any? %>
  <p style="margin:0 0 6px;font-size:13px;color:#666;">Busiest Vertos in that window</p>
  <table style="border-collapse:collapse;margin:0 0 16px;font-size:14px;">
    <% @rows.each do |row| %>
      <tr>
        <td style="padding:4px 16px 4px 0;"><%= row[:name] %></td>
        <td style="padding:4px 16px 4px 0;color:#666;"><%= row[:organisation] %></td>
        <td style="padding:4px 0;text-align:right;"><%= row[:responses] %></td>
      </tr>
    <% end %>
  </table>
<% end %>

<p style="margin:0 0 16px;font-size:14px;">
  Nothing is wrong. This is a heads-up that something is happening, so there is
  time to scale the web service up by hand if it keeps climbing — the service
  has a persistent disk, so it cannot autoscale.
</p>

<p style="margin:0;font-size:13px;color:#666;">
  One of these per <%= @window_minutes %> minutes for as long as the rate stays above the
  threshold (<code>TRAFFIC_ALERT_PER_MINUTE</code>).
</p>
